  "counting": {
    "forward_cite": "FRCP 6(a)(1)",
    "roll_cite": "FRCP 6(a)(1)(C)",
    "backward_cite": "FRCP 6(a)(5)",
    "extension_mode": "after_roll",
    "note": "Exclude the day of the event, count every day, include the last day; a last day on a Saturday, Sunday or legal holiday runs to the next day that is not one (6(a)(1)(C)). Rule 6(d) adds 3 days after the period would otherwise expire under 6(a), and the result rolls again. Counting backward, the next day is the day before (6(a)(5)). State holidays count as legal holidays for forward periods under 6(a)(6)(C); this engine reports them and does not take that extension unless --state-holidays is set."
  },
